# Draft knowledge entry: eigenpy should expose the exact Boost.Python Conan component
id: DRAFT-eigenpy-boost-python312-component-linkage
trigger_tool: conan|cmake|package_info
phase: package_info|configure
error_signature: "boost::boost|boost::python312|cpp_info.requires|CMakeDeps|Python_INCLUDE_DIRS|Python_LIBRARIES|find_dependency(Python)"

severity: 2
category: eigenpy|boost|python312|conan
match_keywords: eigenpy, boost::python312, cpp_info.requires, CMakeDeps, Boost.Python, Python_LIBRARIES, Python_INCLUDE_DIRS

title: eigenpy package_info should require the exact Boost.Python Conan component
root_cause: >
  eigenpy links Boost.Python as part of its runtime surface. If package_info only
  exposes a broad Boost dependency, downstream CMakeDeps consumers may miss the
  exact Boost.Python component and end up with ambiguous linkage. During OHOS
  cross-builds, Boost.Python's generated config also calls find_dependency(Python),
  so the recipe must pass the same Python executable, include dir, and libpython
  path through legacy PYTHON_* and modern Python/Python3 CMake variables.
affected_scope: >
  eigenpy 3.13.0 HarmonyOS PC recipes and similar Conan packages that consume
  Boost.Python through CMakeDeps.
verification_cmd: |
  conan export archives/e/eigenpy/3.13.0 --user=ohpcd --channel=stable
  conan graph info archives/e/eigenpy/3.13.0 --user=ohpcd --channel=stable --format=json
  sh "$HOME/bin/run-ohos-shadow-ci.sh" archives/e/eigenpy/3.13.0

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: expose-boost-python-component-directly
rec_description: >
  Set self.cpp_info.requires to ["eigen::eigen", "boost::python312"] after the
  recipe has validated the Boost.Python package. Pass Python executable,
  include, and libpython hints into both CMake command-line definitions and a
  top-level preload file so nested Boost.Python dependency discovery resolves
  Python 3.12 consistently. Keep the existing early configuration guard so the
  recipe still fails clearly when the resolved Boost package does not provide
  libboost_python312/libboost_python3/libboost_python.
rec_command: |
  self.cpp_info.requires = ["eigen::eigen", "boost::python312"]
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-package-info-boost-python312

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: fail-fast-when-boost-python-component-is-missing
fallback_description: >
  If the selected Boost package does not expose the required Python component,
  stop with a clear ConanInvalidConfiguration error rather than letting CMake
  discover the mismatch later.
fallback_command: |
  raise ConanInvalidConfiguration("boost/1.90.0.2.1 package does not contain Boost.Python for Python 3.12")
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: conan-fail-fast-boost-python

extra_priority: 3
extra_approach: preload-python-cmake-cache-for-boost-python
extra_description: >
  Populate PYTHON_LIBRARY, Python_LIBRARIES, Python3_LIBRARY, and
  Python3_LIBRARIES from the libpython found beside the selected interpreter.
  This prevents Boost.Python's find_dependency(Python) from rediscovering an
  incomplete Python installation during OHOS cross-build configure.
extra_command: |
  set(Python3_LIBRARIES "<device-python-libpython>" CACHE FILEPATH "" FORCE)
extra_auto_fix: false
extra_impl: ohos-python-cmake-preload

forbid_1_pattern: "cpp_info\\.requires\\s*=\\s*\\[.*boost::boost.*\\]"
forbid_1_reason: A Boost.Python consumer must advertise the exact Boost.Python component, not just the umbrella Boost package.
forbid_1_consequence: Downstream CMakeDeps consumers can miss the Python component target and produce ambiguous or incomplete linkage.

principles: exact-component-linkage, fail-fast-on-missing-boost-python, pin-python-cmake-cache
source_event: eigenpy/3.13.0 HarmonyOS PC main adaptation after Boost.Python dependency merge
last_updated: 2026-08-29
